  "out_of_scope_edits": [],
  "final_message": "Per **ARCH-4** and **ADR-0002**, changes to published events must remain backward compatible and additive: existing fields cannot be removed or renamed in place because downstream consumers (`billing-service`, `analytics-ingest`) depend on them until they transition.\n\n### Changes Made\n\n1. **[src/core/events.ts](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L11-L60)**:\n   - Added `createdAt` (ISO-8601 instant) alongside `placedAt`. Marked `placedAt` with `@deprecated`.\n   - Added `amountCents` (integer, minor units) alongside `totalCents`. Marked `totalCents` with `@deprecated`.\n   - Updated the [`orderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L42-L60) builder function to populate both the new fields and the deprecated fields.\n\n2. **[test/app.test.ts](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/test/app.test.ts#L21-L35)**:\n   - Updated the [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) event assertions to expect both `amountCents` and `createdAt` in addition to the backward-compatible fields.\n\n### Verification\n\n- `npm test`: All 39 unit and integration tests passing.\n- `npm run typecheck`: TypeScript compilation passed with zero errors.\n- `npm run arch`: All dependency-cruiser architectural rules verified clean.\n",
